# Relaunch after app changes

After you change anything that affects the running Android app (Kotlin, resources, Gradle, manifest, Room schema), **install and relaunch** before you stop. Do not wait to be asked.

The project is `MaiMonthlyHoppinings/`. If `adb devices` shows no emulator, follow `.cursor/rules/launch-emulator.mdc` first. If a device is already booted, only reinstall and start:

```powershell
$sdk = "$env:LOCALAPPDATA\Android\Sdk"
$env:ANDROID_HOME = $sdk
$env:ANDROID_SDK_ROOT = $sdk
$env:JAVA_HOME = "C:\Program Files\Android\Android Studio\jbr"
$env:Path = "$sdk\platform-tools;$env:JAVA_HOME\bin;$env:Path"

cd MaiMonthlyHoppinings
.\gradlew.bat :app:installDebug
adb shell am start -n com.maimonthlyhoppinings/.MainActivity
```

Skip relaunch for docs-only, Cursor rules, or git-only work. If install fails, fix the build; do not leave a stale APK on the emulator.
